# Task 147-012: AgentRoutingHealth Detector

## Approach

### Files to Create
1. `src/nervous/detectors/agent-routing.ts` — AgentRoutingHealth detector class
2. `tests/nervous/detectors/agent-routing.test.ts` — 8 test cases

### Implementation Plan

#### agent-routing.ts (~250 LoC)
- Class `AgentRoutingHealth` with `detectorId = 'agent-routing'`
- Only triggers on `sprint-lifecycle` source + `SPRINT_PHASE_CHANGE` + `newPhase=EVALUATE`
- Reads .tasks/*.json files from projectRoot
- Detection 1: Corrupt agent validation (AGENT_ID_REGEX = /^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*[a-z0-9]$/)
  - Note: 'a' is too short (needs at least 2 chars) — regex requires [a-z0-9] at end after [a-z0-9-]*
  - Actually DIRECTIVES says 'a' is too short — min length 2 chars
- Detection 2: Anomaly (>= 40% of tasks assigned to same agent)
- Returns severity='critical' if any corrupt-agent issues, else 'warning'

#### Test Cases
1. No tasks → null
2. Valid agents only, no anomaly → null  
3. 1 task with agent='string;' → corrupt-agent, severity='critical'
4. 1 task with agent='a' (too short per regex) → corrupt-agent
5. 14/17 tasks test-writer (82%) → anomaly warning
6. Sprint 146 replay: 9/17 test-writer + 1 'string;' → 2 issues, severity='critical'
7. Wrong phase (not EVALUATE) → null
8. Corrupt + anomaly mix → severity='critical'

### Key Design Decisions
- AGENT_ID_REGEX = /^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*[a-z0-9]$/ — requires min 2 chars, alphanumeric start/end
- Anomaly threshold default = 0.40
- FS mocking needed for tests (readdirSync, readFileSync, existsSync)
